In the community of the [[The Battle Cats]], the term '''cheese''' refers to strategies that allow players to clear stages in ways that were unintended by [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]], usually by taking advantage of the varying enemy limit present in every [[Battle|battle]].

==Ways to Cheese==
==='''Sniping the Base'''===
All battles can only be won by destroying the enemy base, usually after most of the threats are gone. However, some [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] (e.g., [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]], [[Splendid Ganesha (Uber Rare Cat)|Splendid Ganesha]], [[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]]) are able to hit foes a certain distance ahead of their target, which enables them to reach the base even when there are still enemies guarding it, and can destroy it altogether if kept alive long enough. Naturally, this method is harder to pull off in stages with high base HP or [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|enemy Long Distance attackers]] (e.g., [[Mr. Mole]], [[Hackey]], [[Loris]]), as most LD attackers don't inflict much damage.

This cheese is also possible with some cats that don't have Long Distance such as [[Nekoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Unknown Cat]] or [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]], due to their massive range, but it's easier with Long Distance attackers because they don't have to reach the base in order to hit it. Alternatively, units that possess extreme Omni Strike range (such as [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]] and [[The 10th Angel (Uber Rare Cat)|The 10th Angel]]) can also be used, as Omni Strike units will stop at their max range when near the enemy base, even if their usual standing range is shorter, thus allowing them to start whittling the base from afar.

A slight variation of this cheese involves filling the enemy limit with peons, then using Long Distance Cats with big enough blind spots and long enough piercing range to hit the base but not the peons. Using [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]] is a good way to keep the peons in front of the base without reaching your Long Distance attackers. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]]'s Normal Form and Golfer Cat work well at not hitting the peons, as Nerd Cat has a single-target attack, and [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer]]'s standing range is well within his blindspot.

==='''Rushing'''===
The main threats of many stages only appear after the battle has been on for some time, which means the player doesn't have to fight them if they manage to somehow clear the stage by destroying the base before said threats spawn. Doing this is also necessary to receive certain [[Timed Score Reward]]s.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Electrosafari]], [[Inspirational Mural]], [[High Watchtower]], [[Urura (Cats of the Cosmos)|Urura]] and [[Heavenly Tower]] [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 41|Floor 41]]

==='''High-Speed Clip Cheese'''===
One of the hardest and least practical methods of cheesing, this one takes advantage of the fact that units lose their hitboxes for a few frames when they're in their knockback animation. All the player needs to do is use [[Sniper the Cat]], the [[Cat Cannon]] (against enemies vulnerable to Waves), Holy Blast (against Zombies) or Breakerblast (against enemies vulnerable to knockback) to force the enemy to flinch, allowing a fast unit like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]] to clip past it and get to the enemy base without having to kill the main enemy. The only reason why this isn't more popular is because it can take over an hour of practice to get the timing right, making it generally impractical.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Forest Beasts (Deadly)]], [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30 (Heavenly Tower)]], [[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Parade of the Dead]], [[Steel Visage (Deadly)|Steel Visage]].

==='''Li'l Tank Cat Cheese'''===
[[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Tank Cat]] (or [[Ancient Egg: N206 (Special Cat)|Clam Cat]] if you have it) has the shortest range of any [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]], at 100. Incidentally, many of the weaker peons—[[Doge]], [[Snache]], [[Those Guys]], [[Baa Baa]], [[Croco]], [[B.B.Bunny]], [[Squire Rel]], [[Doge Dark]], [[UltraBaaBaa]] and [[Croconator]]—stand at just above 100 range.

What this means is that if Li'l Tank Cat gets to the enemy base and the peons consist of the ones mentioned above, the enemies will stand ''slightly behind'' their base, opening a path for stronger units to quickly destroy it '''if the enemy limit is full.''''' In stages with more buffed peons, the player may need to use Li'l Tank Cat's [[True Form]], Li'l Eraser Cat.

If any cat with longer range than Li'l Tank Cat is used instead, the peons will stand in front of the base and eventually die to the player's attackers, freeing up the enemy limit for the main threats.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Tapas Desert]], [[Marco Po Road]], [[A Boat Too Far]], [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]].

==='''Stacking Ms. Signs'''===
[[Ms. Sign]] is an enemy that spawns in almost every stage, usually every 15 minutes, but a few stages ([[Chubby B. Goode]], [[Last Gang]], [[Murmuring Evil]], [[Gouache Ghouls]]) spawn her earlier than that. Despite having high enough health (10,000) to survive against most meatshields, getting knocked back up to 10,000 times, and standing at double the range of [[Le'boin]], she deals almost no damage with her attacks.

Because of Ms. Sign's unusual attributes listed above, the player can easily knockback a group of Ms. Signs after slowly stacking them up on meatshields, filling the enemy limit, and open a path for attackers to destroy the base without spawning the boss. This takes ''hours'' in most stages where it can be done, even with a [[Speed Up]] enabled, so it should only be used as a last resort, unless in stages like [[Gouache Ghouls]], where it is mandatory to do so.

Ms. Sign is not present in most Merciless-[[Stage Difficulties|difficulty]] stages (including the vast majority of [[Uncanny Legends]] stages), possibly because of this very strategy.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Dark Souls (Insane)|Dark Souls]], [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]], [[Heaven's Oasis]].

==='''Exploiting Target Only'''===
As the ability's name suggests, the Target Only ability limits a cat to attacking certain types of enemies, along with enemy bases. This means that if the player has a unit who can't hit the initial peons, they can wait for the peons to stack up in front of the enemy base and fill the enemy limit, then use the Target Only Cat to hit the base without also killing the peons. [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]] is a great choice for this because of their Base Destroyer ability. If one does not have him, [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Takeda Shingen]] will suffice, due to his already insane base damage.

Incidentally, almost none of the currently existing [[:Category:Focused Target Cats|Target Only Cats]] target [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless Enemies]], making this easiest to pull off on stages that don't have any traited enemies at the beginning.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Lots O' Lion (Deadly)|Lots O' Lion]].

==='''Kubilan Pasalan's Knockback'''===
[[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kubilan Pasalan]]'s abilities combined with his low damage output allow him to gradually knockback enemies until they are behind the base, allowing the player to attack it with impunity. In stages where bosses spawn on base hit, it's possible to avoid fighting the boss altogether if the initial threats clog up the enemy limit. Because this cheese relies on Kubilan Pasalan's low attack power, it's recommended that the player keeps him at a low level unless they want to unlock his [[True Form]].

This also can work with [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]] if one does not have Kubiluga. While Cat God's attack cycle is significantly longer and may end up killing the peons, he can still act as a source of chip damage and whittle down the enemy base.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Benzene Field]], [[Mineral Treatment]], [[Last Labyrinth]], [[Bell Collector]], [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 32|Floor 32 (Heavenly Tower)]]

=== Long-Distance / Wave Stacking ===
This strategy relies on the first part of a stage having limited or weak peons, allowing one to infinitely stall and stack up Long Distance units, often to make the stage significantly easier. This is most often done with [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] since his attack hits outside of his standing range, however this is possible with other units like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]]. Weak metals, such as [[Metal Hippoe]] and [[Croconator]], are also ideal choices since they have enough health to withstand many hits and don't push much on their own.

A more niche variant involves using an [[UltraBaaBaa]] to stack wave attackers on. This is only possible due to UltraBaaBaa's comically strong barrier of 266,000 for how easily she is stalled by meatshields.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Haunted Genome]], [[Lifesaving Shovel]], [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 48|Heavenly Tower Floor 48]]

==='''Healer Perma-Freeze'''===
[[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] is normally unremarkable even for a CC unit due to his long recharge time, poor survivability, horrible speed and low range. However, he has a 100% chance to Freeze non-Metal enemies for 3 seconds. With an attack frequency of 4.63 seconds, Healer requires the support of a Freeze Up M Combo and all relevant Treasures for a targeted trait maxed (which means Traitless, Relic and Aku enemies cannot be permanently frozen) to reach full uptime. While difficult to pull off, a well-timed Healer can perma-Freeze certain threats, making them much more manageable, especially if they have only one knockback, as they will not be able to escape Healer's Freeze on their own.

A variation of this strategy is used on certain Heavenly Tower stages with [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] with Traitless bosses, as Tourist's knockback helps to recover ground with a Freeze effect covering Healer's downtime.

Examples of stages cheesable with this method: [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]], [[Manbosaki Strikes!/Sudden Death Lv.1~20|Manbosaki Strikes]], [[Heavenly Tower]]'s [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]]/[[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]]/[[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]], [[Tiny Wings (Deadly)|Tiny Wings]], [[Flappy Cat (Insane)|Flappy Cat]] and [[Forest Beasts (Deadly)|Forest Beasts]]

